SOAPBOX: Condition were not great, but given the scoring format of this contest that is not immediately a disaster. It just limits the contest to essentially a 2 band affair: 20 and 40m ... On Sunday, 15m was a bit better than Saturday but raising a decent run was not possible with my station. Even snagged a few SA prefixes on 10m. Fortunately 20 and 40 were great and I could run for long times. Did some S&P in the wee periods to collect a few more prefixes. I took plenty of time off, so spent about 25 hours on the air. In the scoring list I see hams doing "every QSO is a multiplier" (e.g. OE5TXF). That seems to be an interesting category to practice your S&P skills ... Maybe make it an official category ?
SOAPBOX: Huge thanks to my host Roy, PD8RW, for making his station available to me. He lives in the countryside and the noise level is so much lower that at my home station, making it much more joyful to operate ... Thanks for organizing and thanks to all who called me.
